From: FlaxAdvisors
Subject: Fix SEGV in AllowlistFilter when prov-mode-mgr is not running

When prov-mode-mgr is absent, postInit() returns early after catching
std::out_of_range from map.at(), leaving restrictedMode as an empty
vector. filterMessage() then calls restrictedMode[hostIdx] (operator[]
with no bounds check) on an empty vector<bool>, causing a SEGV on every
local (system interface) IPMI command.

Fix: guard with a size check so that if restrictedMode was never
populated, the filter simply passes all commands through.

--- a/whitelist-filter.cpp
+++ b/whitelist-filter.cpp
@@ -228,7 +228,8 @@
     size_t hostIdx = request->ctx->hostIdx;

     if (request->ctx->channel == ipmi::channelSystemIface &&
-        restrictedMode[hostIdx])
+        hostIdx < restrictedMode.size() &&
+        restrictedMode[hostIdx])
     {
         if (!std::binary_search(
             allowlist.cbegin(), allowlist.cend(),
